# The four data/*.json files are written by scripts/generate.mjs and
# scripts/apply-feedback.mjs running in GitHub Actions on Ubuntu, so they're
# always committed with LF line endings. Without this, a Windows checkout
# (with core.autocrlf=true, the common Windows Git default) converts them to
# CRLF locally, which then makes git think they're "modified" relative to
# what's committed -- even when the actual content is identical -- and can
# block a pull/merge with a false "local changes would be overwritten"
# error. Forcing eol=lf here keeps them LF on every platform, matching what
# Actions always commits, so this class of false conflict stops recurring.
data/*.json text eol=lf
